law.text:
		The Commissioner may revoke any permit issued pursuant to this article whenever he determines that:

The waterworks can no longer be depended upon to furnish pure water;


The capacity of the waterworks is inadequate for the purpose of furnishing pure water;


The owner has failed to abide by an order issued by the Commissioner;


The owner has abandoned the waterworks and discontinued supplying pure water; or


The owner has failed to pay the waterworks operation fee required by § 32.1-171.1.
